# .public-surface-allow - justified exceptions to scripts/public-surface-check.
#
# One rule per line, four fields:
#
#     category | path-glob | reason | pattern
#
# A rule masks exactly the text its pattern matches, only under the paths its
# glob matches, only for its category. Everything else on the same line is
# still checked. Patterns use %HH hex escapes where spelling a term in full
# would otherwise trip the guard's own scan of this file.
#
# Run `scripts/public-surface-check --help` for the full syntax.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public API this repository exists to publish.
#
# The removed medallion.connect.v1 package remains a public historical
# contract name in the archived proof and migration documentation. Both
# dotted and underscored forms identify that contract. The space-separated brand phrase is not: it names a product rather
# than the published package, and it stays off this surface.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
codename | * | the removed public package named by archived proof and migration documentation | %6dedallion[._]connect
codename | * | the one service in that public package, as the generated bindings and descriptor name it | %6dedallionconnect[a-z]*service

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retired names that survive only as schema reservations. A reservation is the
# record that a field number and name are permanently spent, so it is the fix
# for the retired name, not a leak of it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
retired-scope | archive/connect-v1/projection/medallion/connect/v1/connect.proto | a reserved name in the schema is what permanently retires it; removing the reservation would let it be reused | reserved "organi%7Aation%5fid"
